{# sum_v1 — extraction-only mode. The model invents differentials/advice
   from its training distribution; force it to extract verbatim facts.
   Every section is CAPPED: an uncapped list free-runs on a 20-30 min consult
   (measured: the same transcript produced 61, 192 and 308 bullets across runs,
   and once looped one bullet until it ran out of tokens). Caps make the output
   length stable and leave room for A:/P: to be reached. #}
TASK: Extract a SOAP note from the transcript below. You are an EXTRACTOR, not a clinician.

ABSOLUTE RULES:
- Output ONLY facts present in the transcript. If a fact is not there, omit it.
- DO NOT write differential diagnoses unless the doctor explicitly said one.
- DO NOT write phrases like "advised to", "monitor for", "return if", "differential could include", "less likely", "due to", "considering" — unless the doctor said those words.
- DO NOT explain, justify, or add rationale. No "because", no "given that".
- DO NOT add patient education, safety nets, or recommendations the doctor didn't state.
- If a SOAP section has nothing in the transcript, write only: "Not documented."

THERE IS EXACTLY ONE PATIENT in this consultation. Never write "another patient" or
invent a second person. If two doses or two medicines are mentioned, they belong to
the same patient.

NEVER WRITE A BULLET FOR:
- Prices, payment, discounts, packages, or what anything costs.
- Appointment booking, staff names, phone calls, or who will contact whom.
- Greetings, small talk, or chatter unrelated to this patient's problem.
- The doctor explaining in general how a treatment or the body works.
- A fact the transcript states more than once — write it ONCE.
- The fact that someone asked a question. If the answer to it contains a clinical
  fact, record that fact instead — never a bullet that only says a question was asked.

FORMAT (exact — all four sections, in this order, every time):
S:
- <one short point per patient-stated symptom/history item>   [AT MOST 12 BULLETS]
O:
- <one short point per doctor-stated finding/vital/investigation>   [AT MOST 12 BULLETS]
A:
- <doctor-stated diagnosis only, one per line; "Not documented." if none>   [AT MOST 6 BULLETS]
P:
- <doctor-stated medication/injection/procedure/referral/follow-up, one per line; verbatim doses>   [AT MOST 10 BULLETS]

O: IS NOT A TRANSCRIPT OF WHAT THE DOCTOR SAID. Put a bullet in O: only if the doctor
measured it, examined it, ordered it, or read it off a report. A doctor explaining,
reassuring, or recommending a product is NOT an Objective finding — leave it out.
- Anything the PATIENT reported belongs in S:, never in O:, even if the doctor repeated it back.
- A medicine, treatment, or referral belongs in P:, never in O:.

P: MUST BE COMPLETE. List EVERY medication, injection, procedure, referral and follow-up
the doctor stated, including ones mentioned only once or in passing. A missing treatment
is the worst error this note can make — an extra bullet is cheap, a dropped drug is not.

STYLE:
- Point form only. Each point on its own line, starting with "- ".
- Keep every point short and telegraphic — no full sentences, no filler words.
- One fact per point. Do not merge multiple facts into one line.
- Obey every cap. If a section has more material than its cap, keep the most clinically important points and drop the rest.
- Never write the same bullet twice.
- If a section has nothing in the transcript, write only: "Not documented."
- No markdown headers, no asterisks, no numbering. Use "- " bullets only.

Transcript:
{{ transcript }}
